 Core Docker Configuration Files Future users can inspect or modify how the containers build by reviewing these specific project files: A. The Production Entry point (render.yaml)To ensure Render compiles the app using the exact internal settings shown above, the deployment engine is locked to the runtime: docker definition:
# yaml
services:
  - type: web
    name: azure-cost-dashboard
    runtime: docker           # ◄── Enforces Docker compilation over raw code
    dockerfilePath: ./Dockerfile
    plan: free
#
B. The Client User Interface (frontend/Dockerfile)The frontend uses a multi-stage build script to keep the final image size incredibly small:
#
Stage 1 (Build): Pulls a lightweight node:22-alpine footprint, installs dependencies via npm ci, and compiles your React assets into static files inside a /dist folder.
#
Stage 2 (Production Host): Discards the heavy Node engine, pulls a secure nginx:alpine image, drops your compiled /dist files into Nginx's public web folder, and hosts the UI on port 3000.
#
C. The API Application Layer (backend/Dockerfile)The backend pulls a safe node:22-alpine foundation, maps its active environment to port 3001, and sets up an isolated system directory partition at /app/logs to protect live operational files.